# YOLO26n through Ignition's own pipeline against AMD's stack: 3.41x, and 8.91 mAP more accurate
# Host DESKTOP-CBL5NUA (Desktop 2, Ryzen 7 8700G, XDNA1 Phoenix), 2026-09-21, Device 0.
# Ignition in its balanced default through live_ignition.py; AMD's stack through
# tools/amd_vitisai_yolo.py on Ryzen AI 1.7.1's Phoenix 4x4 xclbin. Arms alternating, two rounds,
# 50 warm-up and 500 timed frames of bus.jpg. xrt-smi idle before every run and after the last.
#
## Why this sitting exists
#
# Every YOLO26 latency published before this came from tools/bench_container_vs_amd.py, whose
# decode is deliberately unoptimized numpy ON EVERY ARM. That is a fair container comparison and
# it read 2.49x. It is not an Ignition number and no badge could carry it. This is the pipeline.
#
# The ratio MOVED, and upward: the pipeline decodes in 0.092 ms where the benchmark charged the
# engine arm about 4.5 ms of numpy. AMD's arm gained too (its decode fell from 5.270 to 1.254 ms)
# but by less, because its frame is dominated by session.run.
#
## Result
#
# | arm                              | run 1  | run 2  | mean    | vs AMD |
# |----------------------------------|-------:|-------:|--------:|-------:|
# | AMD Ryzen AI 1.7.1, Vitis AI EP  | 37.437 | 37.672 |  37.555 |      - |
# | Ignition, sigmoid epilogue       | 11.033 | 11.011 |  11.022 |  3.41x |
# | Ignition, no epilogue (control)  | 10.725 | 10.714 |  10.720 |  3.50x |
#
# Ignition with the epilogue is 3.41x AMD's stack, 26.533 ms faster per frame.
# The epilogue costs +0.303 ms (2.8% of the frame), which agrees with the
# +0.260 ms the container benchmark measured for it independently.
#
## Accuracy is NOT from this sitting
#
# 32.55 mAP@50-95 for the epilogue container against AMD's 23.64, over all 5,000 COCO val2017
# images, was measured by pipelines/yolov8n/5_eval_map.py and is recorded in
# results/aie/yolo26n_silu_recovery_20260921.log and yolo26n_coco_map_20260921.log. The model's
# own float export scores 39.66 on that harness, so 32.55 is 7.11 BELOW float: the win is against
# AMD on the same quantized weights, not against the float model.
#
## Detections
#
# The epilogue container returns 5.00 objects per frame on bus.jpg and the control 6.00, on every
# one of 500 timed frames in both rounds. AMD returns 6. The sixth is a quantization artifact of
# the HardSigmoid form which the float model does not produce either, so 5 is the correct count.
# Ignition took its boxes from the NPU detect heads on 500/500 frames in all four engine runs.
#
## What was NOT established here
#
# - AMD's EP placement. Both AMD runs printed 'EP report node devices report not found', so the
#   12-of-1,526-nodes figure is the earlier session's and is not re-confirmed by this one.
# - Energy. Not measured for any arm.
# - AMD's first run paid a 26.61 s session load and the second 0.56 s; G2G excludes both.
#
